1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,540
Hey, Black Power, what's the reaction to your arrest, Mr. Brown?

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:03,380
Of course.

3
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:08,960
Wait since America has done it again, but that's not going to end the burning in burning in Detroit, brother,

4
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:12,040
because we built the country up and we'll burn it down, honkies and all.

5
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:14,340
Mr. Brown, did you tell them to burn down that school?

6
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:15,300
Be serious.

7
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,000
I ain't got to tell black folks what to burn.

8
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:18,780
Did you tell them to shoot Lady Bird?

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,460
Did I tell them to burn down Detroit?

10
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:23,420
Did I tell them to bring black people here?

11
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:25,420
Did you tell them to shoot Lady Bird?

12
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:27,960
I say they give me a gun and tell me to shoot my enemy.

13
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:28,820
I might shoot you.

14
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:30,520
Where have you been since the other night, baby?

15
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:32,220
Oh, well.

16
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:35,300
But a lot of you running around talking about you Democrats,

17
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:37,920
and the Democrats got you in the biggest trick going.

18
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,780
They tell you that our fault is the Dixocrats.

19
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:42,560
There's no such thing as the Dixocrats.

20
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:47,000
The only difference between George Wallace and Lyndon Johnson is one of them's wife got cancer.

21
00:00:49,210 --> 00:00:54,050
He works off the military-industrial complex, which means that it's profitable to wage war.

22
00:00:54,050 --> 00:01:00,710
And unless you, you know, devise another plan or another scheme to sustain or to boost this economy,

23
00:01:01,150 --> 00:01:08,250
then it's going to be necessary to wage war, whether, you know, a black individual is in office or a white individual is in office.

24
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:12,070
So we're talking about a complete change in system.

25
00:01:12,070 --> 00:01:19,310
If Mr. Cleaver did win the election, don't you think that he could have conducted the presidency in a unique manner

26
00:01:19,310 --> 00:01:23,190
that may not be, you know, compromising to the system you speak of?

27
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:28,030
No, because, as I said, the system dictates the response to individuals.

28
00:01:28,030 --> 00:01:36,490
You see, individuals do not influence, you know, politically, economically, or socially the attitudes of functioning of the system.

29
00:01:37,390 --> 00:01:42,510
Well, if politics as we know it here in this country is not the answer, what is?

30
00:01:42,670 --> 00:01:45,610
I think there has to be a re-evaluation of politics.

31
00:01:46,150 --> 00:01:49,310
Now, there are definitions of politics that are relevant to black people.

32
00:01:49,750 --> 00:01:54,910
Chairman Mao says that politics is war without bloodshed, and war is an extension of politics.

33
00:01:54,910 --> 00:01:59,190
I think black people have to begin to address themselves to the politics of revolution.

34
00:01:59,850 --> 00:02:03,910
Because we are caught up in a revolutionary struggle, whether we want to believe it or whether we want to be or not.

35
00:02:04,770 --> 00:02:08,870
So I think, you know, black people have to begin to think in a revolutionary fashion

36
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:13,210
and create and construct a politically revolutionary platform.

37
00:02:13,390 --> 00:02:19,350
People recognize, and the poor people recognize first, what it takes to get the man off your back,

38
00:02:19,490 --> 00:02:21,090
what it takes to get freedom in America.

39
00:02:21,090 --> 00:02:23,270
I say violence is necessary.

40
00:02:23,270 --> 00:02:26,350
Violence is a part of America's culture.

41
00:02:26,570 --> 00:02:28,710
It is as American as cherry pie.

42
00:02:29,210 --> 00:02:31,770
American taught the black people to be violent.

43
00:02:32,010 --> 00:02:37,790
Each time a police officer shoots and kills a black teenager, that is urban crime.

44
00:02:37,890 --> 00:02:43,270
Black people have to begin to identify with the word black and with other black people, not Negroes.

45
00:02:44,110 --> 00:02:46,030
You don't decide what I am.

46
00:02:46,030 --> 00:02:50,770
You see, animals and slaves are named after and by their masters.

47
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:52,290
Men named themselves.

48
00:02:52,490 --> 00:02:55,210
Hey, hey, hey, hey, baby, all right!

49
00:02:55,410 --> 00:02:58,890
Better way to enslave a man than give him the vote and call him free.

50
00:02:59,530 --> 00:03:06,010
See, it does not profit black people or poor people anything to have the vote and not be able to select the candidates who they want to choose.

51
00:03:06,010 --> 00:03:12,630
Now, how can you choose between London, Johnson, Nixon, Agnew, Wallace, and Humphrey?

52
00:03:13,030 --> 00:03:14,210
There is no choice.

53
00:03:14,850 --> 00:03:15,610
Evil is evil.

54
00:03:15,750 --> 00:03:16,730
There's nothing in between that.

55
00:03:16,730 --> 00:03:19,230
There were some lesser candidates.

56
00:03:19,550 --> 00:03:21,890
Gregory was running for office.

57
00:03:22,390 --> 00:03:23,130
Eldridge Cleaver.

58
00:03:23,770 --> 00:03:27,630
I think the vote can only be used as a tool of organization.

59
00:03:27,810 --> 00:03:29,810
We can only use the vote to organize our people.

60
00:03:30,390 --> 00:03:38,010
Now, to really believe that we can put someone in office and that these people would be responsive to our needs is naive, politically naive.

61
00:03:38,010 --> 00:03:47,510
Because even if one of the black candidates who ran for office were to take the office of president, then black people must be prepared to fight against that person.

62
00:03:48,110 --> 00:03:51,430
Because, you see, the system mandates the action of the individual.

63
00:03:51,970 --> 00:03:54,530
The individual does not determine how this country will function.

64
00:03:54,950 --> 00:04:00,110
This country works off the military-industrial complex, which means that it's profitable to wage war.

65
00:04:00,110 --> 00:04:09,570
And unless you, you know, devise another plan or another scheme to sustain or to boost this economy, then it's going to be necessary to wage war.

66
00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:14,290
Whether, you know, a black individual is in office or a white individual is in office.

67
00:04:14,630 --> 00:04:18,130
Well, we're talking about a complete change in system.

68
00:04:18,730 --> 00:04:23,070
You see, we recognize America for what it is, the Fourth Reich.

69
00:04:23,470 --> 00:04:29,790
And we tell America to be on notice because if you are going to play Nazis, black folks ain't going to play Jews.

70
00:04:35,330 --> 00:04:37,290
DC and Baltimore, you're up next.

71
00:04:38,170 --> 00:04:43,870
I'm outside, y'all, doing what I can to decolonize minds on my mission-driven book tour for my new book, What Would the Ancestors Say?

72
00:04:46,410 --> 00:04:48,750
They say books won't change the world.

73
00:04:49,370 --> 00:04:51,850
Tell that to every colonizer that burned them.

74
00:04:52,090 --> 00:04:55,070
Come on out, be in community, buy a book, and get it signed.

75
00:04:55,530 --> 00:04:57,410
RSVP at amandaseals.com

